---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ReturnToBuddy from '../components/ReturnToBuddy.astro';
---
<Layout title="Buddy vs DeepSeek-R1 — Measured, Hash-Sealed — AIIT-THRESI" description="A direct, hash-sealed benchmark: Buddy vs DeepSeek-R1-Distill on the identical Qwen2.5-14B base, same machine, same 50 prompts. ~4.6x faster, ~10x fewer tokens, equal-or-better accuracy. Same answer, far less waste.">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section style="padding-top:140px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--gold);">⬡ Measured · Hash-Sealed · AIIT-DISC-0001</div>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(44px,7vw,104px); margin-bottom:22px; line-height:1.0;">
        Same answer.<br><span style="color: var(--amber);">Forty times less.</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="color: var(--ink-soft); font-size:21px; max-width:820px; line-height:1.55; margin-bottom:34px;">
        We asked Buddy and DeepSeek-R1 the same simple question — on the <strong>identical 14B base model, the same machine, the same 50 prompts.</strong> Both got it right. One carried far less waste.
      </p>

      <!-- THE PARIS HOOK -->
      <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border:1px solid #233047; border-radius:16px; padding:28px 30px; max-width:860px;">
        <div style="font-family:'Courier New',monospace; color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:14px; margin-bottom:18px;">"What is the capital of France?"</div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; margin-bottom:6px;">
            <span style="width:60px; color:var(--gold); font-weight:700;">Buddy</span>
            <span style="height:18px; width:3%; min-width:10px; background:#5a6b82; border-radius:4px;"></span>
            <span style="color:var(--ink); font-size:15px;"><strong>7 tokens · 2.0s</strong> → "Paris."</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px;">
            <span style="width:60px; color:var(--gold); font-weight:700;">R1</span>
            <span style="height:18px; width:100%; max-width:460px; background:#5a6b82; border-radius:4px;"></span>
            <span style="color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:15px;"><strong>279 tokens · 7.3s</strong> → "Paris."</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:15px; border-top:1px solid #233047; padding-top:14px;">
          Both got <strong style="color:var(--ink);">"Paris."</strong> R1 used ~40× the words and ~3.6× the time to say it.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SCOREBOARD -->
  <section style="padding-top:64px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--teal);">The scoreboard · 50 frozen prompts</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px); margin:10px 0 24px;">Not theory. <span style="color:var(--amber);">Measurement.</span></h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
      <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:15px; color:var(--ink-soft);">
        <thead><tr style="background:#0f1626; color:var(--ink);">
          <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 12px;">Measured</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 12px; color:var(--gold);">Buddy-14B</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 12px; color:var(--gold);">R1-Distill-14B</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 12px;">What it means</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Mean latency</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">3.8 s</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">17.4 s</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;"><strong>~4.6× faster</strong></td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740; background:#0d1422;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Worst-case (p95)</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">7.4 s</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">38.3 s</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">~5.2× faster</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Tokens / answer</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">59</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">621</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">~10× fewer (mean); ~40× on a simple answer</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740; background:#0d1422;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Accuracy*</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">95%</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">85%</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">equal-or-better (*small n — see note)</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Sycophancy (folds under pressure)</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">~8%</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">~6%</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;"><strong>tie</strong> — tiny n, both hold</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740; background:#0d1422;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Reasoning depth</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">not optimized</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">deeper, by design</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;">likely R1's edge — <em>not benchmarked</em></td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #1c2740;"><td style="padding:10px 12px;">Base model</td><td style="padding:10px 12px; color:var(--amber);">Qwen2.5-14B</td><td style="padding:10px 12px; color:var(--amber);">Qwen2.5-14B</td><td style="padding:10px 12px;"><strong>identical</strong> — every gap is what each team added</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      <p style="color:#8493a8; font-size:13px; margin-top:12px;">*Accuracy: first-try on keyed science MC — Buddy 38/40, R1 17/20. R1's run was capped at n=20 because its per-answer latency (5–40 s) made longer runs costly — not a sample-bias choice. Sycophancy denominators are tiny (3/38 vs 1/17) → "tie within noise," not a robust win.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THREE LENSES -->
  <section style="padding-top:56px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--teal);">Three lenses · one fact</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.5vw,40px); margin:10px 0 8px;">The same efficiency, three ways to see it</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); max-width:760px; margin-bottom:24px;">Brevity is a resource advantage — and on real hardware it compounds.</p>
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr)); gap:18px;">
        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid #233047; border-top:4px solid var(--amber); border-radius:14px; padding:22px;"><div style="color:var(--amber); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Tokens</div><div style="font-size:26px; color:var(--ink); font-weight:700;">~10× / ~40×</div><div style="color:#8493a8; font-size:14px;">aggregate / per simple answer — for engineers</div></div>
        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid #233047; border-top:4px solid var(--amber); border-radius:14px; padding:22px;"><div style="color:var(--amber); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Water-drops 💧</div><div style="font-size:26px; color:var(--ink); font-weight:700;">7 vs 279</div><div style="color:#8493a8; font-size:14px;">if each token were a drop — intuitive</div></div>
        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid #233047; border-top:4px solid var(--amber); border-radius:14px; padding:22px;"><div style="color:var(--amber); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">Joules &amp; °C 🌡️</div><div style="font-size:26px; color:var(--ink); font-weight:700;">14 J vs 2,567 J</div><div style="color:#8493a8; font-size:14px;">+10°C vs +27°C, measured on the GPU</div></div>
      </div>
      <p style="color:#8493a8; font-size:13px; margin-top:14px;">GPU energy is one measurement, board-watts only (not whole-datacenter cooling/water); consumer single-inference. Directional magnitude, not a precise constant.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COST ASYMMETRY -->
  <section style="padding-top:56px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--teal);">The asymmetry</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.5vw,40px); margin:10px 0 18px;">One person. One consumer GPU.</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); max-width:820px; line-height:1.6;">
        Buddy was built by <strong>one person</strong> over <strong>57 active development days</strong> — ~355 wall-clock hours, ~142 verified GPU-training hours, a consumer RTX 3090-class workstation, ~20 TB of Starlink-routed data, limited cloud bursts. <strong>Capital basis ~$5,525–5,770; direct operating cost ~$784–884.</strong> DeepSeek-R1-Distill is distilled from a 671B frontier-lab teacher trained on a GPU cluster — we cite no dollar figure for it and fabricate nothing. The asymmetry is the point: <strong style="color:var(--amber);">frontier results don't require frontier budgets — they require the right architecture.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SEAL + DOWNLOAD -->
  <section style="padding-top:56px; padding-bottom:40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid #233047; border-radius:16px; padding:28px 30px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold);">⬡ Provenance</div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); margin:8px 0 16px; line-height:1.55;">Every number here is tied to a measured run or the build log; the frontier-lab side is reported-only. The full report and all raw data are <strong>hash-sealed</strong> — entry <strong>AIIT-DISC-0001</strong> in the AIIT Discovery Ledger, evidence&nbsp;sha256 <code style="color:var(--amber); font-size:13px;">c76adc8c…</code>.</p>
        <a href="/buddy-vs-r1-technical.html" style="display:inline-block; background:var(--gold); color:#0a0a12; font-weight:700; padding:13px 26px; border-radius:10px; text-decoration:none;">Here's the technical details →</a>
        <a href="/buddy-vs-r1.pdf" style="display:inline-block; margin-left:14px; color:var(--gold); font-weight:600; text-decoration:none; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(200,144,64,0.45); padding-bottom:2px;">Download the sealed PDF →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:34px;"><ReturnToBuddy /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
